                "observations": [
                    "test/recognise.test.mjs:1279 The late-timer test proves the wake schedule is deadline-aligned, not that the shown value comes from the deadline: a mutation that keeps the deadline-aligned wake but decrements a counter per callback passes all 40 tests (verified on dist). With late=900 every callback still lands in the right second. A late value over 1000 ms (a skipped second) would separate the two.",
                    "src/recognise/recognise.ts:824 next.focus() runs without {preventScroll:true}. After a pointer tap in Chrome/Android the tapped button holds focus, so the redraw moves focus by script. The :focus-visible heuristic should keep the ring hidden, and iOS Safari does not focus tapped buttons, so there is no effect there. Not checked on a device: possible scroll-into-view, and a screen reader announcing the newly focused button over the polite status line (fits card NG-48 item 3)."
